Table full name: bigquery-public-data.new_york_taxi_trips.tlc_green_trips_2020
Column name: vendor_id Type: STRING Description: A code indicating the LPEP provider that provided the record. 1= Creative Mobile Technologies, LLC; 2= VeriFone Inc.
Column name: pickup_datetime Type: TIMESTAMP Description: The date and time when the meter was engaged
Column name: dropoff_datetime Type: TIMESTAMP Description: The date and time when the meter was disengaged
Column name: store_and_fwd_flag Type: STRING Description: This flag indicates whether the trip record was held in vehicle memory before sending to the vendor, aka 'store and forward,' because the vehicle did not have a connection to the server. Y= store and forward trip N= not a store and forward trip
Column name: rate_code Type: STRING Description: The final rate code in effect at the end of the trip. 1= Standard rate 2=JFK 3=Newark 4=Nassau or Westchester 5=Negotiated fare 6=Group ride
Column name: passenger_count Type: INT64 Description: The number of passengers in the vehicle. This is a driver-entered value.
Column name: trip_distance Type: NUMERIC Description: The elapsed trip distance in miles reported by the taximeter.
Column name: fare_amount Type: NUMERIC Description: The time-and-distance fare calculated by the meter
Column name: extra Type: NUMERIC Description: Miscellaneous extras and surcharges. Currently, this only includes the $0.50 and $1 rush hour and overnight charges
Column name: mta_tax Type: NUMERIC Description: $0.50 MTA tax that is automatically triggered based on the metered rate in use
Column name: tip_amount Type: NUMERIC Description: Tip amount. This field is automatically populated for credit card tips. Cash tips are not included.
